      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A prospective, randomised and independently assessed trial of the Ring UPM total hip replacement showed that the quality of the early result was better if the femoral prosthesis was cemented than if it was not. More patients with cemented prostheses were painfree at four months (58% cemented:42% uncemented) and at one year (63% cemented:50% uncemented), but at two years pain relief was equal in both groups. At two years significantly more patients with cemented prostheses could walk without support (96% cemented:62% uncemented, p = 0.01 to 0.05). There is a need for more similar trials to compare the results of contemporary designs of cemented and uncemented total hip prostheses."},
